      en: {
        metaTitle: "Taxi Clermont Airport to Le Mont-Dore | 55 min €70",
        metaDescription: "Taxi from Clermont Airport to Le Mont-Dore: 60 km in 55 min from €115. Puy de Sancy ski and spa resort. Flight tracking, mountain vehicle. Fixed fare booking.",
        heroTitle: "Taxi Clermont Airport → Le Mont-Dore",
        heroSubtitle: "Your Clermont Airport → Le Mont-Dore transfer at €115 — €140. 60 km, Puy de Sancy and skiing.",
        description: "The taxi transfer from Clermont-Ferrand Auvergne Airport to Le Mont-Dore is the fastest way to get from the plane to the ski slopes or historic thermal baths. In 55 minutes through the volcanic landscapes of the Sancy, your mountain-specialist driver takes you directly to the foot of the Puy de Sancy, the highest point of the Massif Central at 1,886 metres.",
        routeDescription: "The route joins the A71 from the airport before branching onto the D2089 towards Le Mont-Dore via Rochefort-Montagne. The journey gradually crosses the Volcanoes Park landscapes, passing from the Limagne plains to the mountainous Sancy terrain. The final descent into Le Mont-Dore offers a magnificent panorama of the snow-covered massif in winter or lush green in summer, with the Puy de Sancy dominating the horizon.",
        introduction: "Le Mont-Dore is a dual resort: both a historic Massif Central ski station and a renowned thermal spa since Gallo-Roman times, nestled at 1,050 metres altitude at the foot of the Puy de Sancy (1,886 m), the highest point in the entire French Massif Central. Clermont-Ferrand Auvergne Airport (CFE) is the ideal air gateway to reach Le Mont-Dore: in a 55-minute taxi transfer, you go from the air terminal to the heart of the resort, whether for a ski holiday, thermal cure or summer hiking break. The Mont-Dore – Sancy ski domain offers 31 runs over 41 km, served by 14 ski lifts, with often excellent snow coverage thanks to the altitude and north-facing exposure. The resort is particularly popular with families and intermediate skiers for the variety of its runs, from gentle green plateau runs to technical black runs in the Val de Courre. The Sancy cable car goes directly to the summit of the Puy de Sancy, offering 360° views over the Auvergne volcanoes, Cantal mountains and, on clear days, the Alps. The Mont-Dore thermal baths, whose origins date back to the Roman occupation, are among France's oldest. The current establishment, built in the 19th century in spectacular neo-Byzantine style with mosaics, columns and painted vaults, offers 18-day conventional cures specialising in respiratory conditions (asthma, chronic bronchitis) and rheumatology. The thermal springs emerge at 44°C, rich in silica, bicarbonates and arsenic at therapeutic concentrations. The airport taxi transfer is particularly suited to skiers arriving with bulky equipment: skis, snowboards, boots, luggage... Our vehicles have spacious boots and roof racks on request. In winter, road equipment is crucial: access roads to Le Mont-Dore pass through cols above 1,000 metres that can be snowy or icy. Our drivers, accustomed to these conditions, drive vehicles systematically equipped with approved snow tyres and carry chains when needed. They know alternative routes if a road is closed and can provide real-time updates on resort snow conditions.",
        itineraire: "Your driver collects you at the single terminal of Clermont-Ferrand Auvergne Airport with a name board. The route first takes a short stretch of the A71 to bypass Clermont to the south, then branches onto the D2089, the main road to the Sancy. The road passes successively through Royat, Saint-Genès-Champanelle and the volcanic plateau with spectacular views of the Chaîne des Puys. After Rochefort-Montagne, a mountain market town with its Romanesque church, the road plunges into the upper Dordogne valley. The descent to Le Mont-Dore is a highlight: the Sancy massif gradually reveals itself with its jagged ridges, glacial cirques and, in winter, its snow cover heralding the slopes. Arrival is via the north of the resort, passing the first chalets and hotels. Tolls approximately €2 (included in the fare). Allow 55 min under normal conditions, up to 1h10 in winter depending on snow.",
        conseils: "Share your flight number when booking for real-time tracking. Free waiting up to 45 min if delayed. In winter, our vehicles are fitted with snow tyres and chains — you have no worries. Buy your ski passes online in advance from the Mont-Dore resort website to skip the queue. The ski area generally opens mid-December to late March (adult day pass €35, child €28). The Mont-Dore thermal baths offer conventional cures and discovery wellness packages from €30. In summer, the Sancy cable car (return €12) is the starting point for the Massif Central's finest hikes. If arriving with skis, mention it when booking so we can arrange a vehicle with roof rack if needed.",
        comparaisonTransport: "There is no direct shuttle between Clermont-Ferrand Airport and Le Mont-Dore. Public transport: airport shuttle to Clermont (20 min, €5) then Transdôme bus to Le Mont-Dore (1h30-2h, €8) with often lengthy connections: allow 2h30 to 3h30 minimum, plus managing skis and luggage between vehicles. Airport car rental: €45-70/day, but mountain roads in winter require special equipment. The taxi at €115-140 offers a direct, comfortable, safe 55-minute transfer with an expert mountain driver and equipped vehicle. For 3-4 passengers (€18-30/person), the most rational solution.",
        faq: [
          { question: "Does the driver wait for me at Clermont Airport?", answer: "Yes, your driver waits with a name board in the arrivals area. They track your flight in real time and adapt to any early or late arrival of your plane." },
          { question: "How much is the airport to Le Mont-Dore transfer?", answer: "The fixed fare is €70 to €90 depending on time and day, tolls included. Price guaranteed at booking with no surcharge for luggage or ski gear. Van rate (up to 7 passengers): €120." },
          { question: "Can the vehicle access Le Mont-Dore in deep winter?", answer: "Absolutely. Our vehicles are systematically fitted with snow tyres from November to April, and drivers carry chains for the most challenging conditions. They know the Sancy roads intimately in all conditions." },
          { question: "Can we transport skis in the taxi?", answer: "Yes, our boots are spacious and can accommodate several pairs of skis. For groups with lots of gear, mention this when booking and we'll arrange a vehicle with roof rack or a van." },
          { question: "Is a return to the airport possible?", answer: "Yes, book the return at the same fixed fare. Your driver collects you from Le Mont-Dore at the agreed time based on your departure flight, with comfortable safety margin." },
          { question: "Is Le Mont-Dore open in summer too?", answer: "Yes, Le Mont-Dore is a four-season resort. In summer: Sancy cable car, hiking (GR 30, GR 4), mountain biking, thermal baths open year-round. The resort is as beautiful for summer hiking as for winter skiing." },
          { question: "Can I combine Mont-Dore skiing and visiting La Bourboule?", answer: "Absolutely. La Bourboule is just 10 km from Le Mont-Dore. Your driver can drop you at either resort, or arrange a shuttle between the two during your stay." },
          { question: "Are flights from Paris to Clermont frequent?", answer: "Clermont-Ferrand Auvergne Airport has regular flights from Paris-Orly several times daily, plus links to Lyon and seasonal destinations. Ideal for a Sancy ski weekend." },
        ],
      },
